6,Kuranko language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kuranko_language,"The Kuranko language is a member of the Mande branch of the Niger-Congo language family, one of the major phyla of African languages spoken primarily in West Africa. Within this family, Kuranko is classified under Western Mande, specifically within the Mokole subgroup, which forms part of the broader Central Mande division.",Kuranko,Niger-Congo
